course: dictionary
lesson: 4895
title: Roman numerals: III
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: III is a Roman numeral. Romans used letters for numbers, and we still see them on clocks, in history books and in story titles. III is written with three I's, and it means 3.
explain: Each letter has a value: I = 1, V = 5 and X = 10. So III is 1 + 1 + 1 = 3. Read the letters to add up their values.
explain: After a name, III means «the third». «Henry III» is said «Henry the Third». The numeral tells you which king with that name he was.
explain: III can also number a part of a book or story. «Chapter III» is the third chapter, so the number shows the order.
fact: III is the Roman numeral for 3.
fact: III is written with three I's, and each I is worth 1.
fact: On a clock, III marks three o'clock.
fact: «Henry III» is said «Henry the Third».
fact: Some clocks show 4 as IIII, because clockmakers liked how it looked.
exercise: What number is III? | 13 | *3 | 4 | 2
exercise: «Chapter III» starts the third part of a story. What does III mean here? | The first chapter | *The third chapter | A chapter with three pages
exercise: On a clock, which hour does III mark? | Nine o'clock | *Three o'clock | Twelve o'clock | Six o'clock
test: What number is XII on a clock? | 2 | *12 | 6 | 10
test: Which Roman numeral means 6? | XII | IV | *VI | IX
exam: «King Charles III» reigns today. What does III tell you about him? | Charles has three children | Charles is three years old | *Charles is the third king with that name | Charles lives at number three
